  <prompt>Execute the Phase F E2E acceptance per spec.md FR-18 + SC #5 + design.md §15: provision a fresh trial-{yyyymmdd} customer stamp using the Model 1 profile via the new pipeline invoked through /provision-environment skill. Verify: (a) Setup Status transitions to Ready; (b) all 6 §4B silent-fail traps (T1-T6) cleared by owning handler post-conditions; (c) all 5 §4D tenant-isolation invariants (I1-I5) sample-verified; (d) scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1 exits 0 on r1-owned surfaces; (e) cost envelope conforms per §15 #14 targets (Model 1 marginal ≤ $430/mo, shared platform floor ≤ $400/mo); (f) Model 1/2 handler behavior differences per §4.1a verified (Model 1 dry-run minimum; Model 2 dry-run if reasonable). Publish full E2E verification report at projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/phase-f-e2e-acceptance-2026-XX-XX.md.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform senior engineer + operator. Expert in the full 19-handler pipeline (H0..H14), L2 REST + reconciler operation, §4B trap catalog + §4D invariant enforcement, cost envelope measurement via Azure Cost Management, and E2E verification-report authoring. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>A fresh trial-{yyyymmdd} customer stamp exists in dev Azure with Model 1 profile; Setup Status = Ready in Dataverse; all 6 §4B traps verified cleared; all 5 §4D invariants sample-verified; naming-conformance-check.ps1 exits 0; cost envelope report shows conformance to §15 #14 targets. Verification report at projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/phase-f-e2e-acceptance-2026-XX-XX.md documents every check + verdict + supporting evidence.</goal>

  <context>
