  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load spec.md FR-18 + SC #5 + SC #6 + §4B + §4D + §15 #14 + design.md §15.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Prereq check">Verify all dep tasks (057-088) status = ✅ in TASK-INDEX.md; verify /provision-environment skill is invocable.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Model 1 provision">Invoke /provision-environment with customerId=trial-{yyyymmdd}, tenancyModel=Model1Shared, profile=trial. Walk through skill Step 0 → completion; capture handoff report.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Setup Status check">Query sprk_dataverseenvironment for the trial customer; verify sprk_provisioning_setupstatus = Ready.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Trap verification">For each of T1-T6, run the trap-verification query (per §4B) against the trial stamp; document result per trap.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Invariant verification">Sample-verify each of I1-I5: (I1) grep provisioning scripts for tenant-shaped defaults; (I2) sample AI Search query; (I3) sample Cosmos query; (I4) verify SPE container-ID resolution; (I5) verify Graph token per-tenant scope.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Naming conformance">Run `pwsh -File scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1 -Scope r1-owned`; expect exit 0.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Cost envelope">Query Azure Cost Management API for the trial stamp's RG + shared-tier resources; compare against §15 #14 targets.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Model 2 dry-run">Discretionary — if reasonable in dev budget, provision a second stamp with tenancyModel=Model2Dedicated + verify §4.1a differences hold; else document skip rationale.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Report">Write notes/phase-f-e2e-acceptance-2026-XX-XX.md with per-check verdict + evidence + Setup Status screenshot equivalent + cost report + Model 2 result-or-skip.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Cleanup">Discretionary teardown OR leave trial stamp for reference (per plan.md Phase F Deliverables).</step>
    <step order="11" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 089 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="12" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ANY trap OR ANY invariant OR cost drift &gt;20% fails, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5 rather than lowering the threshold or silently proceeding. Phase F acceptance is BINDING — a fail here blocks task 090 wrap-up. Owner input required on remediation path (path A exception documented; path B ADR amendment; path C fix + re-run).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">Invoke skill + scripts</tool>
    <tool name="az">Query Azure resources + Cost Management</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Verify BFF + L2 build/test</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

